{
    "TrueVision__UserSpellings__Meta": {
        "Meta__FileName"    : "TrueVision__UserSpellings__.json",
        "Meta__Description" : "The TrueVision spelling dictionary: the words the spell check in TrueVision's text boxes accepts that the browser's own dictionary does not know - manufacturers, product names, stone and quarry names, construction terms, abbreviations and the practice's software. Read by 02__Src__AppModules/55__Feature__SpellCheck; written by hand, and by Add to Dictionary through the ProjectVision local server (na-apps/ProjectVision__TrueVisionUserConfig__Api__.py).",
        "Meta__Version"     : "1.0.0",
        "Meta__Created"     : "22-Sep-2026",
        "Meta__Author"      : "Adam Noble - Noble Architecture",
        "Meta__HowItWorks"  : "The browser's own spell check does the checking, with its own dictionary and its own suggestions (right-click a word it underlines). A word listed here is marked to be skipped wherever it is typed, so it is never underlined. Nothing here is copied into the browser's dictionary, and a word that is ordinary English needs no entry.",
        "Meta__HowToAdd"    : "By hand: put the word in any group's Group__Words, one to a line, spelt and capitalised as it should be written. A new group is a copy of a group block with its own Group__Key and Group__Title. In the app: put the caret in the word in a spell-checked box and press Add to Dictionary - it lands in the AddedInTheApp group, which the app keeps in alphabetical order and is the only group it writes to.",
        "Meta__Matching"    : "A word is accepted in any case (VELUX, Velux, velux), with 's after it (Velux's) and with a plural s or es (rooflights for rooflight). An entry of several words - Farrow & Ball, Jeld-Wen - accepts each of its words. A word is letters and digits, with an apostrophe inside it if it needs one."
    },

    "TrueVision__UserSpellings__UpdatedIso": "2026-09-22T09:00:00.000Z",

